  "construction_notes": [
    {
      "text": "From the state Housing Element Annual Progress Report, through 2025.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001136",
        "SRC-001148"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Coastal Commission staff report: two buildings, a four-unit building facing Beach Blvd and a three-unit building inland, on a vacant parcel. Appellants were GRG/Pacific Ventures, Ltd. and Nicholas Langhoff. Staff recommended substantial issue and approval with a 105-foot coastal hazard setback, which it expected to cut the project to about 3 to 4 units. The report lists the APN as 016-011-019.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-004144"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Coastal Commission staff report: a prior nine-unit condominium project on this parcel (CDP A-2-PAC-07-022, Pacific Beach LLC/Weng) was approved by the Commission in 2008; its city permits expired October 2016 and its Commission CDP expired March 2017, after which the owner sold the site to the current applicant.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-004144"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Surfrider Foundation reports the Coastal Commission denied the entire proposal in a 6-5 vote on 2020-06-10. The state report's 2022 row says the project was denied by the Coastal Commission and the city could not issue a building permit; its 2023 and 2024 rows say 'permit ready to be issued'.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-004143",
        "SRC-001148"
      ]
    }
  ],
